  "estimatedMinutes": 2,
  "statement": "If \\(p,\\) \\(q,\\) and \\(M\\) are positive numbers and \\(q\\lt100,\\) then the number obtained by increasing \\(M\\) by \\(p\\%\\) and decreasing the result by \\(q\\%\\) exceeds \\(M\\) if and only if",
  "answerChoices": [
    {
      "label": "A",
      "text": "\\(p\\gt q\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "B",
      "text": "\\(p\\gt\\frac q{100-q}\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "C",
      "text": "\\(p\\gt\\frac q{1-q}\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "D",
      "text": "\\(p\\gt\\frac{100q}{100+q}\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "E",
      "text": "\\(p\\gt\\frac{100q}{100-q}\\)"
    }
  ],
  "answer": {
    "letter": "e",
    "value": null
  },
  "solutions": [
    {
      "id": "sol.ahsme-1981-p12.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "The final amount is \\[ M\\left(1+\\frac p{100}\\right) \\left(1-\\frac q{100}\\right). \\] It exceeds \\(M\\) exactly when \\((100+p)(100-q)\\gt10000.\\) Expanding gives \\(p(100-q)\\gt100q.\\) Since \\(100-q\\gt0,\\) this is \\(p\\gt\\frac{100q}{100-q}.\\)\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is E.",
      "hints": [
        "Write the two successive percentage changes as multiplication factors",
        "Use \\(q\\lt100\\) when dividing by \\(100-q\\)"
      ],
      "images": []
    }
  ],
